# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Windows batch files MUST keep CRLF line endings, stored verbatim in the repo.
#
#  Why `-text` (and not `text eol=crlf`)?
#    cmd.exe fails to resolve `goto` labels in LF-only batch files and the
#    window closes instantly. Storing the CRLF bytes as-is guarantees the file
#    works whether it arrives via `git clone` **or** a ZIP/tarball download
#    (GitHub archives do not apply eol conversion).
#
#  Encoding rule: batch files must be UTF-8 **without BOM**. A BOM is read as
#  part of the first command (`@echo off` -> "not recognized"), and the files
#  switch the console to UTF-8 themselves with `chcp 65001`.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.bat -text
*.cmd -text

# Shell scripts are the opposite: LF only, normalized on checkout.
*.sh text eol=lf
